D3D11 MSAA sample-count clamp (DXMT).

Author: Tim Isaev
Applies to: third_party/src/dxmt at e520fea415ba4b82b0c346dae77bbb1be4897453

Why
  DXMT reports D3D_FEATURE_LEVEL_11_0, and 11_0 guarantees 8x MSAA for every
  render target format except R32G32B32A32.  A conformant title may therefore
  ask for 8 samples without calling CheckMultisampleQualityLevels first, and
  Deus Ex: Mankind Divided does exactly that while initializing Scaleform.
  Apple silicon does not go past 4 - measured on this M2 Pro, sample counts 1,
  2 and 4 are supported and 8 is not - so CreateMTLTextureDescriptorInternal
  returned E_INVALIDARG, the title wrapped it in a C++ exception and died
  before its first frame.

  CheckMultisampleQualityLevels1 itself is honest: it consults
  supportsTextureSampleCount and reports 0 quality levels for 8.  The gap is
  that the feature level advertised one layer up promises what the device
  cannot do.

What it does
  Clamps an unsupported sample count down to the highest the device supports
  and reports it once, instead of failing the creation.

  This renders with fewer samples than the title asked for.  That is a visible
  difference and is why it is logged rather than done silently - but it is the
  honest end of a promise already made by advertising 11_0.

Effect
  Deus Ex: Mankind Divided reaches its -benchmark scene and sustains ~73 FPS
  over 20,213 presents with no non-ok DXMT event.  See
  ../results/2026-07-25-08-deus-ex-msaa-clamp.md.

